The numbered terms below are what actually apply; this summary is only a guide.


1. Definitions

"Commercial use" means using something to make money, or as part of anything that
makes money, in any way: selling it, charging to download, play or access it, putting
it behind a paywall or subscription, adding purchases or advertising, offering it on a
paid store listing, using it in paid work or for a business, or streaming or recording
it in a way that earns money from it beyond what section 2.3 allows.

"Permission" means permission given in writing by BiggyStudios.


2. What you may do

2.1 Read and study. You may read the Game's source and study how it works, for your
own learning.

2.2 Build and play. You may build the Game from this repository and play it yourself,
on your own devices.

2.3 Show it. You may show yourself playing the Game in videos, streams and
screenshots, and talk about it, including on channels that earn money in general, as
long as you don't sell or charge for access to the Game itself.

2.4 Fork on GitHub. If this repository is public, you may fork it on GitHub, as
GitHub's terms allow, and make changes in your fork to suggest them back to the Game.
A fork may not be released, shared or used as a game of its own.


3. What you may not do

Unless you have Permission:

3.1 You may not make any Commercial use of the Game, or of any part of it, changed or
unchanged.

3.2 You may not share, upload, publish, distribute or release copies of the Game or
any part of it, whether unchanged, changed, renamed, reskinned or rebranded, whether
you charge for it or give it away for free. GitHub forks under 2.4 are the only
exception.

3.3 You may not use the Game's code, scenes, shaders, textures, models, sounds,
story, characters, setting or writing in any other game, project, book, film or
product, commercial or not.

3.4 You may not make games, mods, remakes, sequels, fan versions or other works
based on the Game, its story or its characters and release them.

3.5 You may not use the Game, or any part of it, to train or improve machine learning
or AI models.

3.6 You may not remove or change this license or the copyright notice, or claim to
have made the Game.


4. Other uses

For anything this license doesn't allow, ask BiggyStudios through the repository on
GitHub. Permission is only given in writing, and only for what it says.


5. Ending

If you break this license, your rights under it end at once, and you must stop using
the Game and delete any copies you made under it.


6. No warranty

The Game is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
